VA = ["element","v1_location","verdict","rationale","evidence_label","source_ids","proposed_by"]
va = [
["Profession families (F1-F15) as the unit of mobility analysis","Dimension Tags F1-F15; Profession Family View; profession_family_definitions.md","change","Families are disciplinary identities, not jobs or sector-actor contexts, so family similarity cannot answer the charter's question (movement between federal, state, local, Tribal, NGO, private and academic). The CM computation finds a two-island structure: a biophysical/field-science cluster (F1-F7, F10, F12) and a statecraft/human-systems cluster (F8, F9, F11, F13-F15) with ZERO pairs above chance between them (33 above-chance pairs, all within clusters; partition identical in 150/150 Louvain runs). Keep families as navigation groupings of role profiles (agrees with CA); compute mobility on role profiles with sector-actor variants","E","CM-003|CM-005|CM-071","CM"],
["Core tag definition ('a meaningful gap'; boundary tests for distinctiveness)","profession_family_definitions.md Core/Supporting distinction","change","For mobility use, Core encodes what is DISTINCTIVE to a professional identity, so Core-only similarity systematically understates transferability by design. Core-only rankings correlate only 0.51 (Spearman) with Core+Supporting rankings. v2 role profiles need importance and level per task, not distinctiveness, so overlap measures reflect what the job actually requires","E","CM-003|CM-005","CM"],
["Supporting tags","Dimension Tags F1-F15 (755 Supporting assignments)","needs-evidence","Supporting tags carry most of the transferability signal (structure is stable at Supporting weight 0.25-0.75, Spearman >=0.99) but were assigned by one analyst with an LLM and no reliability check. Do not migrate as role requirements; use only as a prior to be re-elicited with importance ratings","E","CM-003","CM"],
["Zero-Core / Foundational Professional Preparation flag","Dimension Tags Zero Core; Foundational Professional Prep","change","The idea is right and matters for mobility: 3.1.1-3.1.3 (project planning, budget, risk) are Core in no family yet Supporting in 10, the broadest portable foundation in v1. Re-express as a computed breadth/portability score on role profiles (agrees with CA's 'compute, don't store'). Note that 2 of the 3 carry CLD flags","E","CM-003|CM-071","CM"],
["Domain 7 cross-cutting competencies as bridges","Competencies 7.1.1-7.2.3; Dimension Tags","carry","The seven D7 competencies are the top 7 bridges (54% of 'cross-community core bridges'). Carry them into the transversal layer, but do not cite their bridging as evidence of portability: they were tagged across many families by design (Feb 2026), so the bridging is partly constructed","E","CM-003|CM-071","CM"],
["Sector application notes (5 per competency)","Competencies: Public Agencies | Private Sector | NGOs | Consulting | Academia","change","Agrees with CA (retire structure, keep as seed text). Mobility-specific addition: all 1,110 cells are populated, so every competency claims to apply in every sector. The notes carry zero discriminating information for transferability and cannot be used to compute sector-actor similarity","E","CM-003|CM-004|CM-071","CM"],
["CLD (career-ladder destruction) flag and R9 severity","Dimension Tags T13 CLD Flag / CLD Severity; CLD Signal Register","change","Carry the concept and compute it per pathway (agrees with CA). Mobility linkage v1 did not draw: CLD concentrates where portability is highest. 37% of SC-primary competencies are flagged vs 20-22% FC/DC; 50% of 'broad foundation' competencies; 36% of the top-25 bridges vs 28% overall. Entry tasks that teach the most portable skills are the most compressed, so CLD is also a mobility risk indicator","E","CM-003|CM-008","CM"],
["Career-ladder position (P/C/X) on tasks","Dimension Tags T13 Tx Career","carry","Needed for entry and progression links on role profiles and for pathway-level CLD (metric M-19). Extend it with sector-actor variants, because entry ladders differ by actor (federal seasonal; corps; consulting junior; state trainee)","J","CM-003|CM-008","CM"],
["Craft primary/secondary as the representation of 'blends'","Dimension Tags Craft Primary / Craft Secondary","change","Agrees with CA (blend profile, not classification). Computation shows blends are asymmetric. Field-management families (F1-F4, F10, F12) have even blends (evenness 0.91-0.99; e.g. Forestry FC 38/DC 38/SC 24) while statecraft-cluster families hold almost no field craft (FC 0.7-7%). The charter's 'blend of three crafts' describes field professionals, not policy, ESG, finance or education professionals in v1's tags","E","CM-003|CM-001","CM"],
["Family -> SOC labor market crosswalk","Labor Market Crosswalk sheet","change","Agrees with CA. Mobility-specific point: validating family similarity against observed occupational flows (CPS, LEHD) needs correct SOC targets; with 7 of 15 mappings rated Low by v1 itself, flow-based validation is infeasible for half the families until role-level SOC/OPM-series/state-class crosswalks exist","E","CM-003|CM-071","CM"],
["Five Functional Positions framework (bridging competencies between information-flow positions)","Five_Functional_Positions_Framework.docx","carry","A useful within-organisation mobility lens (Sensing <-> Structuring <-> Analyzing <-> Integrating <-> Deciding) that v1 never connected to its tags. Carry as a candidate work-function facet for role profiles (CA's L0) and test whether position adjacency predicts internal moves","J","CM-006","CM"],
["Workforce Signals dashboard","Workforce Signals sheet","change","It counts taxonomy outputs (craft distribution, Core counts, reform flags), not workforce outcomes. Replace with outcome and leading-indicator metrics (metrics_framework.csv) so the tool is held to outcomes, not deliverables","J","CM-003","CM"],
["Fire Management <-> Land Use Planning tags","Dimension Tags F9/F12; profession_family_definitions.md overlap notes","needs-evidence","The family definitions name Fire <-> Planning overlap (community wildfire protection planning), yet Fire holds 0 of Land Use Planning's 13 Core competencies and similarity is below chance (z = -1.65). Either the tags omit real overlap or the overlap is in tasks v1 never wrote. Re-check in L2 with fire and planning SMEs; this is a high-demand pathway for displaced fire staff","E","CM-003|CM-005","CM"],
["Delphi panel plan","taxonomy_task_sequence_v7.md Tasks 20-21","change","Agrees with CA (redesign under IO). Add reserved Workforce Voice seats with ratings reported by stratum, and a usefulness veto at G1 (practitioner_panel_design.md)","J","CM-071","CM"],
["Absence of any observed career-path data","whole v1","add","v1 never tested a transferability claim against an observed move. Add consented career histories (panel), state HR prior-employment fields, OPM Federal Workforce Data and licensed career-history data as the validation layer for pathway claims (metric M-03)","E","CM-003|CM-022|CM-023","CM"],
]
w("v1_assessment.csv", VA, va)

